ordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/releases\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/releases: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn3view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/commits/main/\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/commits/main/: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn3view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/main/LICENSE\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/main/LICENSE: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2610.27530] ZKPU: Zero-Knowledge Processing Unit for Heterogeneous Workloads (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.27530)\nciteturn3view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.27530\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 167\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Hardware Architecture\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 20 Oct 2026]\nL9: # Title:ZKPU: Zero-Knowledge Processing Unit for Heterogeneous Workloads\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Jonathan Ku】, 【6†Changchun Zhou】, 【7†Jiawen Wu】, 【8†Sangouk Jeon】, 【9†Cong Guo】, 【10†Yuzhe Fu】, 【11†Bowen Duan】, 【12†Dongsuk Jeon】, 【13†JV Rajendran】, 【14†Yiran Chen】, 【15†Hai Li】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled ZKPU: Zero-Knowledge Processing Unit for Heterogeneous Workloads, by Jonathan Ku and 10 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【16†View PDF】 【17†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:Zero-knowledge proofs (ZKPs) have become a fundamental building block for privacy-preserving computation, blockchain systems, and verifiable machine learning. Modern ZKP protocols span two distinct families: curve-based protocols, which rely on large finite-field arithmetic, and hash-based protocols, which operate over native 64-bit fields.\nL17: Existing hardware accelerators are specialized for one protocol family because they are built on operand-scanning Montgomery multiplication, resulting in fixed-width datapaths, poor utilization across heterogeneous operand widths, and limited scalability.\nL18: > This paper presents \\emph{ZKPU}, a Zero-Knowledge Processing Unit for heterogeneous ZKP workloads. ZKPU introduces a new compute paradigm by co-designing finely integrated product scanning (FIPS) Montgomery multiplication with a reconfigurable Twin Systolic Fabric (TSF), enabling modular multiplication at arbitrary widths in 64-bit increments.\nL19: Combined with a fine-grained Deque buffer, on-chip twiddle-factor generator, and memory-efficient MSM preprocessing strategy, ZKPU provides a unified architecture for both curve-based and hash-based protocols.\nL20: Evaluation using Groth16 and Plonky2 shows that ZKPU achieves up to $144\\times$ speedup for NTT, $13.6\\times$ for MSM, and approximately $7.2\\times$ end-to-end application speedup over state-of-the-art accelerators, while being the first architecture to efficiently support both protocol families on a single reconfigurable hardware platform.\nL21: Subjects:  | Hardware Architecture (cs.AR)\nL22: Cite as:  | 【18†arXiv:2610.27530】 [cs.AR]\nL23:    | (or 【19†arXiv:2610.27530v1】 [cs.AR] for this version)\nL24:    | 【20†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2610.27530†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Jonathan Ku [【21†view email】]\nL28: [v1] Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:47:37 UTC (741 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL3