pyright†info.arxiv.org】 · 【58†Privacy†info.arxiv.org】 · 【59†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org】 · 【60†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org】\nL163: \nL164: Major funding support from\nL165: \nL166: 【61†(opens in new tab)†www.simonsfoundation.org】 【62†(opens in new tab)†www.sfi.org.bm】 【63†(opens in new tab)†www.schmidtsciences.org】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCUDA Runtime API :: CUDA Toolkit Documentation (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/12.8.0/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__MEMORY.html)\nciteturn3view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn1view0\",\"lineno\":2238}); Total lines: 2876\nL2200: ###### Parameters\nL2201: \nL2202: `dst`\nL2203:     - Destination memory address\nL2204: `src`\nL2205:     - Source memory address\nL2206: `count`\nL2207:     - Size in bytes to copy\nL2208: `kind`\nL2209:     - Type of transfer\nL2210: `stream`\nL2211:     - Stream identifier\nL2212: \nL2213: ###### Returns\nL2214: \nL2215: 【188†cudaSuccess】, 【189†cudaErrorInvalidValue】, 【316†cudaErrorInvalidMemcpyDirection】\nL2216: ###### Description\nL2217: Copies `count` bytes from the memory area pointed to by `src` to the memory area pointed to by `dst`, where `kind` specifies the direction of the copy, and must be one of 【317†cudaMemcpyHostToHost】, 【318†cudaMemcpyHostToDevice】, 【319†cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost】, 【320†cudaMemcpyDeviceToDevice】, or 【321†cudaMemcpyDefault】. Passing 【321†cudaMemcpyDefault】 is recommended, in which case the type of transfer is inferred from the pointer values.\nL2218: However, 【321†cudaMemcpyDefault】 is only allowed on systems that support unified virtual addressing.\nL2219: The memory areas may not overlap. Calling 【169†cudaMemcpyAsync()】 with `dst` and `src` pointers that do not match the direction of the copy results in an undefined behavior.\nL2220: 【169†cudaMemcpyAsync()】 is asynchronous with respect to the host, so the call may return before the copy is complete. The copy can optionally be associated to a stream by passing a non-zero `stream` argument. If `kind` is 【318†cudaMemcpyHostToDevice】 or 【319†cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost】 and the `stream` is non-zero, the copy may overlap with operations in other streams.\nL2221: \nL2222: The device version of this function only handles device to device copies and cannot be given local or shared pointers.\nL2223: \nL2224: Note:\nL2225:   * Note that this function may also return error codes from previous, asynchronous launches.\nL2226: \nL2227:   * This function exhibits 【289†asynchronous】 behavior for most use cases.\nL2228: \nL2229:   * This function uses standard 【290†default stream】 semantics.\nL2230: \nL2231:   * Note that this function may also return 【190†cudaErrorInitializationError】, 【191†cudaErrorInsufficientDriver】 or 【192†cudaErrorNoDevice】 if this call tries to initialize internal CUDA RT state.\nL2232:   * Note that as specified by 【193†cudaStreamAddCallback】 no CUDA function may be called from callback. 【194†cudaErrorNotPermitted】 may, but is not guaranteed to, be returned as a diagnostic in such case.\nL2233: \nL2234:   * Memory regions requested must be either entirely registered with CUDA, or in the case of host pageable transfers, not registered at all. Memory regions spanning over allocations that are both registered and not registered with CUDA are not supported and will return CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE.\nL2235: See also:\nL2236: \nL2237: 【154†cudaMemcpy】, 【156†cudaMemcpy2D】, 【162†cudaMemcpy2DToArray】, 【160†cudaMemcpy2DFromArray】, 【157†cudaMemcpy2DArrayToArray】, 【323†cudaMemcpyToSymbol】, 【324†cudaMemcpyFromSymbol】, 【159†cudaMemcpy2DAsync】, 【163†cudaMemcpy2DToArrayAsync】, 【161†cudaMemcpy2DFromArrayAsync】, 【325†cudaMemcpyToSymbolAsync】, 【326†cudaMemcpyFromSymbolAsync】, 【361†cuMemcpyAsync】, 【362†cuMemcpyDtoHAsync】, 【363†cuMemcpyHtoDAsync】, 【364†cuMemcpyDtoDAsync】\nL2238: __host__ ​【116†cudaError_t】 cudaMemcpyBatchAsync ( void** dsts, void** srcs, size_t* sizes, size_t count, 【94†cudaMemcpyAttributes】* attrs, size_t* attrsIdxs, size_t numAttrs, size_t* failIdx, 【149†cudaStream_t】 stream )\nL2239: \nL2240: \nL2241: Performs a batch of memory copies asynchronously.\nL2242: ###### Parameters\nL2243: `dsts`\nL2244:     - Array of destination pointers.\nL2245: `srcs`\nL2246:     - Array of memcpy source pointers.\nL2247: `sizes`\nL2248:     - Array of sizes for memcpy operations.\nL2249: `count`\nL2250:     - Size of `dsts`, `srcs` and `sizes` arrays\nL2251: `attrs`\nL2252:     - Array of memcpy attributes.\nL2253: `attrsIdxs`\nL2254:     - Array of indices to specify which copies each entry in the `attrs` array applies to. The attributes specified in attrs[k] will be applied to copies starting from attrsIdxs[k] through attrsIdxs[k+1] - 1. Also attrs[numAttrs-1] will apply to copies starting from attrsIdxs[numAttrs-1] through count - 1.\nL2255: `numAttrs`\nL2256:     - Size of `attrs` and `attrsIdxs` arrays.\nL2257: `failIdx`\nL2258:     - Pointer to a location to return the index of the copy where a failure was encountered. The value will be SIZE_MAX if the error doesn't pertain to any specific copy.\nL2259: `stream`\nL2260: ###### Returns\nL2261: \nL2262: 【188†cudaSuccess】【189†cudaErrorInvalidValue】\nL2263: ###### Description\nL2264: \nL2265: Performs a batch of memory copies. The batch as a whole executes in stream order but copies within a batch are not guaranteed to execute in any specific order. This API only supports pointer-to-pointer copies. For copies involving CUDA arrays, please see 【166†cudaMemcpy3DBatchAsync】.\nL2266: Performs memory copies from source buffers specified in `srcs` to destination buffers specified in `dsts`. The size of each copy is specified in `sizes`. All three arrays must be of the same length as specified by `count`. Since there are no ordering guarantees for copies within a batch, specifying any dependent copies within a batch will result in undefined behavior.\nL2267: Every copy in the batch has to be associated with a set of attributes specified in the `attrs` array. Each entry in this array can apply to more than one copy. This can be done by specifying in the `attrsIdxs` array, the index of the first copy that the corresponding entry in the `attrs` array applies to. Both `attrs` and `attrsIdxs` must be of the same length as specified by `numAttrs`.\nL2268: For example, if a batch has 10 copies listed in dst/src/sizes, the first 6 of which have one set of attributes and the remaining 4 another, then `numAttrs` will be 2, `attrsIdxs` will be {0, 6} and `attrs` will contains the two sets of attributes. Note that the first entry in `attrsIdxs` must always be 0. Also, each entry must be greater than the previous entry and the last entry should be less than `count`. Furthermore, `numAttrs` must be lesser than or equal to `count`.\nL2269: The 【353†cudaMemcpyAttributes::srcAccessOrder】 indicates the source access ordering to be observed for copies associated with the attribute. If the source access order is set to 【354†cudaMemcpySrcAccessOrderStream】, then the source will be accessed in stream order. If the source access order is set to 【355†cudaMemcpySrcAccessOrderDuringApiCall】 then it indicates that access to the source pointer can be out of stream order and all accesses must be complete before the API call returns.\nL2270: This flag is suited for ephemeral sources (ex., stack variables) when it's known that no prior operations in the stream can be accessing the memory and also that the lifetime of the memory is limited to the scope that the source variable was declared in. Specifying this flag allows the driver to optimize the copy and removes the need for the user to synchronize the stream after the API call.\nL2271: If the source access order is set to 【356†cudaMemcpySrcAccessOrderAny】 then it indicates that access to the source pointer can be out of stream order and the accesses can happen even after the API call returns. This flag is suited for host pointers allocated outside CUDA (ex., via malloc) when it's known that no prior operations in the stream can be accessing the memory. Specifying this flag allows the driver to optimize the copy on certain platforms.\nL2272: Each memcpy operation in the batch must have a valid 【94†cudaMemcpyAttributes】 corresponding to it including the appropriate srcAccessOrder setting, otherwise the API will return 【189†cudaErrorInvalidValue】.\nL2273: The 【365†cudaMemcpyAttributes::srcLocHint】 and 【366†cudaMemcpyAttributes::dstLocHint】 allows applications to specify hint locations for operands of a copy when the operand doesn't have a fixed location. That is, these hints are only applicable for managed memory pointers on devices where 【274†cudaDevAttrConcurrentManagedAccess】 is true or system-allocated pageable memory on devices where 【283†cudaDevAttrPageableMemoryAccess】 is true. For other cases, these hints are ignored.\nL2274: The 【357†cudaMemcpyAttributes::flags】 field can be used to specify certain flags for copies. Setting the 【358†cudaMemcpyFlagPreferOverlapWithCompute】 flag indicates that the associated copies should preferably overlap with any compute work. Note that this flag is a hint and can be ignored depending on the platform and other parameters of the copy.\nL2275: \nL2276: If any error is encountered while parsing the batch, the index within the batch where the error was encountered will be returned in `failIdx`.\nL2277: \nL2278: Note:\nL2279:   * Note that this function may also return error codes from previous, asynchronous launches.\nL2280: \nL2281:   * This function exhibits 【289†asynchronous】 behavior for most use cases.\nL2282: \nL2283:   * Memory regions requested must be either entirely registered with CUDA, or in the case of host pageable transfers, not registered at all. Memory regions spanning over allocations that are both registered and not registered with CUDA are not supported and will return CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE.\nL2284: __host__ ​【116†cudaError_t】 cudaMemcpyFromSymbol ( void* dst, const void* symbol, size_t count, size_t offset = 0, 【155†cudaMemcpyKind】 kind = cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost )\nL2285: \nL2286: \nL2287: Copies data from the given symbol on the device.\nL2288: ###### Parameters\nL2289: \nL2290: `dst`\nL2291:     - Destination memory address\nL2292: `symbol`\nL2293:     - Device symbol address\nL2294: `count`\nL2295:     - Size in bytes to copy\nL2296: `offset`\nL2297:     - Offset from start of symbol in bytes\nL2298: `kind`\nL2299:     - Type of transfer\nL2300: \nL2301: ###### Returns\nL2302: \nL2303: 【188†cudaSuccess】, 【189†cudaErrorInvalidValue】, 【220†cudaErrorInvalidSymbol】, 【316†cudaErrorInvalidMemcpyDirection】, 【221†cudaErrorNoKernelImageForDevice】\n"
